# Build/deploy artifacts and runtime state
engine/zzt-server
engine/zzt-parity
engine/deploy.tar.gz
engine/saves/
test.txt

# M16.1 parity report: a regenerable CI artifact, never committed. The command
# `make parity` (cmd/zzt-parity) writes these; certification is proven by the
# committed manifest, not by this rendered report.
fixtures/parity/report.json
fixtures/parity/report.md
# M16.20 run record: tool versions, the commit, per-gate wall clock, and the
# load run's measured numbers. Deliberately outside the report so two runs of
# one tree still render byte-identical reports; published as a CI artifact.
fixtures/parity/run.json
fixtures/parity/load-metrics.txt

# M12.17 eval runs: keep reports, screenshots, and ZWD sidecars; never the
# generated .ZZT binaries (fixtures are committed as ZWD text only).
llmworld/eval/**/*.ZZT

# Deterministic zzt-build previews are local review artifacts.
llmworld/previews/

# Local agent/project planning notes; keep out of the public repository.
#
# TASKS.md is deliberately NOT in this list even though it is the same kind of
# document. The parity certification tests parse its checked boxes as the
# authority the manifest is verified against (deriveTaskRows in
# engine/parity_manifest_test.go), so three tests fail on a clone that does not
# have it. It ships; see the header at the top of the file.
/ANALYSIS.md
/TASKS-BETA.md
/AWS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/IMPLEMENTATION.md
/NOTES.md
/PLAN.md
/conversion-approach.txt
/ruzzt.txt
/zeta.txt
/engine/errors.txt
